// The 60-second script:
// 'A retain cycle is two objects strongly holding each other, so ARC
//  never deallocates either — a memory leak. The classic case: a view
//  controller stores a closure, and the closure captures the controller.
//  Fix it with a capture list — [weak self] — so the closure holds
//  weakly. Verify in Xcode's memory graph debugger: the purple
//  warning disappears and deinit prints.'

